    "physical_description": "This <font -i>kor</font> (Haka woman's blouse) is made up of two panels (each 28.5 cm wide, complete selvedge to selvedge) which are partially sewn together by hand, leaving holes for the head and arms.\r\n\r\nThe ground fabric is dark red silk with green, blue and white stripes of warp-faced plain-weave bisected across the chest by a band of twill-weave herringbone pattern in yellow, while in the lower section the weft-faced weave dominates. In addition the top portion of the blouse is patterned with tiny geometric designs in white, pale blue and brown silk thread in supplementary weave picked in with a quill. \n",
